{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i128 = __int128_t;\nusing ld = long double;\nusing fraction = pair<long long, long long>;\nusing fraction_set = multiset<fraction>;\n\nlong long b, c, g, n, q, r, t, u, x, y, z;\nmap<ld, fraction_set> container;\n\nvoid save(long long a) {\n    g = std::gcd(a, b);\n    long long num = b / g;\n    long long den = a / g;\n    ld key = ld(std::abs(u - a * z)) / t;\n    container[key].insert({num, den});\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    g = std::gcd(x, y);\n    x /= g;\n    y /= g;\n    q = x / y;\n    r = x % y;\n\n    for (b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n        g = std::gcd(y, b);\n        c = b / g;\n        z = y / g;\n        t = b * z;\n        u = q * t + r * c;\n        save(u / z);\n\n        if (u % z) {\n            save((u + z - 1) / z);\n        }\n    }\n\n    auto outer = container.begin();\n    auto inner = outer->second.begin();\n\n    cout << inner->second << '/' << inner->first;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long b, c, g, n, q, r, t, u, x, y, z;\n    static Map<Double, TreeSet<long[]>> container = new TreeMap<>();\n\n    static long gcd(long a, long b) {\n        if (b == 0) return a;\n        return gcd(b, a % b);\n    }\n\n    static void save(long a) {\n        g = gcd(a, b);\n        long num = b / g;\n        long den = a / g;\n        double key = (double) Math.abs(u - a * z) / t;\n        \n        container.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new TreeSet<>((p1, p2) -> {\n            if (p1[0] != p2[0]) return Long.compare(p1[0], p2[0]);\n            return Long.compare(p1[1], p2[1]);\n        })).add(new long[]{num, den});\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        \n        x = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        y = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        n = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n        \n        g = gcd(x, y);\n        x /= g;\n        y /= g;\n        q = x / y;\n        r = x % y;\n\n        for (b = 1; b <= n; ++b) {\n            g = gcd(y, b);\n            c = b / g;\n            z = y / g;\n            t = b * z;\n            u = q * t + r * c;\n            save(u / z);\n\n            if (u % z != 0) {\n                save((u + z - 1) / z);\n            }\n        }\n\n        Map.Entry<Double, TreeSet<long[]>> outer = container.entrySet().iterator().next();\n        long[] inner = outer.getValue().iterator().next();\n\n        System.out.println(inner[1] + \"/\" + inner[0]);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.794698856538162e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.0014221088495105505, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -0.0339034721255302